  "id": "passive-voice",
  "term": "passive voice",
  "definition": "In this historical source, passive voice is the grammatical form of a verb that presents passivity or the undergoing of an action rather than acting. It is described as the counterpart of an active verb and is linked with Aristotle’s category of passion or passivity.",
